1.31.2: --help rewritten; every option explained

'polajuice --help' said "--ev NUMBER  exposure in stops" at the bottom
of a list headed "Lens and framing", and left out --web. Rewritten:

- grouped by what the options do: the look; exposure and development;
  the light before the camera; lens and framing; files; the options
  only curves, lut and darktable take; raw files; where things are
  found; environment.
- every option says what it does, its range, its default, and which
  way + and - go. --ev: +1 doubles the light reaching the film, acts
  before the film so it moves contrast, saturation and halation with
  the brightness, adds to a raw's built-in stop. --develop: a push adds
  contrast, saturation and grain and does not brighten.
- added what was missing: serve --web, --lens none, --size for
  darktable, the environment variables (POLAJUICE_THREADS,
  POLAJUICE_PROFILE, POLAJUICE_DARKTABLE_CONFIG), the exit status, the
  older spellings (-p/--preset, --lut, 'presets'), a pointer to the
  README's annex on linked controls.
- superjuice --help: --print added; refers to polajuice --help for
  meanings.
- man page: --ev in full, a NOTES section (control identities, older
  spellings).

Test: compat checks that --help mentions every flag the parsers take
and every scene key, and fits 80 columns - so it cannot fall behind
again unnoticed.
